;; The onboarding seat: sits beside one person on their org_plan, first
;; drafts the plan's tree of parts for the person to agree (ticket
;; f9252928), then walks the engine's own audit of it, one finding at a
;; time, turning each into one plain question and writing the code from
;; the answer. Interactive: the person is there. Epic cafa6106, M2d.
{:template
 {:params {:org "The org's name, as its directory under orgs/ spells it: the org_plan's name."
           :repo "The orgs repository the seat writes orgs/<org>/ in and its plan's change opens in: ckopsa/waymark, or a house's own (ticket dce7a672)."}
  ;; the model an org_plan's create holds onboarding-<org> for (ticket 6b49540c)
  :model "claude-opus-5"
  :note "One onboarding seat per org. It writes only under orgs/{{org}}/ in {{repo}}, and reads the kit (orgkit/, orgs/example/, docs/orgkit.md, the factorykit templates) from ckopsa/waymark beside it (R-12.32): bench.edit_many takes no path, so the seat edits one file a call. It walks drafting, simulated and going_live plans: propose leaves drafting, go_live's Allow leaves simulated, and a simulated or going_live plan whose change merged before it was live gets a fresh change at the sit (ticket 87fc7996). It never answers a question, never takes go_live alone (go_live is held for the person, so its call files a held call and the seat's work ends there), and never restates a seat; it holds no live power. The engine moves a proposed plan to simulated once the audit read its change's head, and back to proposed when that head moves."}
 :seat
 {:name "onboarding"
  :mode "interactive"
  :walk "org_plan"
  :cadence_seconds 3600
  :standing_ttl_seconds 604800
  :budget_usd_per_week 10M
  :sitting_budget_tokens 600000
  :sitting_idle_seconds 1800
  :charter "You help one person stand up their org from the brief on your plan row. No parts yet: add the tree by the door create_under names: goal, branches, leaves. Only leaves get a home and home_name; on the rest leave them undecided. A part in the brief's words: source \"stated\", quoting it; else inferred. Tell the person in the conversation the tree is ready: agree, restate and drop are theirs. Code agreed parts under orgs/{{org}} from orgkit; send with change submit. Make each next_step finding one plain question (not \"state overdue has no leaver\" but \"when an invoice is 30 days late, who chases it?\"), ask it on its part, wait: the person answers, never you. Code the answer, submit. Never give a seat more than the person's scope. next_step empty: if org.edn already has an org-mayor seat, propose; else add one at the person's weekly budget, submit, propose. The audit simulates on its next pass (no door). Simulated: set :live true, submit; simulated again: invoke go_live, held for the person's tap; then stop.\n\nHire plan: add an org-seat holding the door out of the gap's state, at the person's budget; submit."
  :instructions "Act; never end a turn on a plan. Your row: waymark_get kind \"org_plan\". No row: ask the person's goal; waymark_invoke kind \"org_plan\", action \"create\", input {name: \"{{org}}\", brief: it}.\n\nTHE TREE: create_under carries plan_part create's input and each home's choices; restate alike. Built-in first: home \"built_in\", home_name off its menu, coded from that docs/orgkit.md section. next_step parts/*: wait.\n\nBENCH: waymark_power (ToolSearch \"waymark_power\" once); each tool's arguments are in bench.inputs. Read docs/orgkit.md, orgkit/, orgs/example/. Edit: bench__edit, `old` from a read; create: true for a new file. Before a submit, bench__check (pending: ask again); fix its findings, [week-*] too. Behind main: bench__pull.\n\nTHE WEEK: orgs/{{org}}/resources/{{org}}/week.edn: day 2 a friction, day 5 the person's tap, day 7 a job delivered and invoiced.\n\nTHE WALK: Submit: waymark_invoke kind \"change\", action \"submit\", input {why}. Submitted: await the findings cue; MCP has no inbox, so read the plan again after 5 min. Red org-findings: bench__feedback, bench__log, fix, submit. Ask only from next_step: action \"ask\", input {key, finding_key, part, question}. No findings: neither ask nor propose. \"Wait for me\" is a :hold, never :decided. Never stall: say why, ask again. Workarounds: \"log_workarounds\".\n\nTHE SEED: cast :owner :id is the plan's owner member id; the first domain's :name is the plan's name. No outside world: :rehearsal {:cast <each sender, :scope creating what they send>, :seats [{:template \"world\"} per world.edn]}, as orgs/example. The mayor: :seats gets {:template \"org-mayor\" :params {:org, :domain, :domain_id [:ref <its domain's :ref>], :owner <that member id>, :budget_usd_per_week <the person's, like 8M; unsaid: ask>, :kinds [{:kind <each org kind> :actions []}], :repos <org.edn's :repos>}}. Propose (no input) only once findings_sha is the change's head. Halted or parked: say why, stop."
  :scope [{:kind "org_plan" :actions ["create" "ask" "log_workarounds" "propose" "go_live" "retire"] :filter {:state "drafting,proposed,simulated,going_live" :name "{{org}}"}}
          {:kind "plan_part" :actions ["create" "restate" "agree" "drop"] :filter {:org "{{org}}"}}
          {:kind "change" :actions ["submit"]}
          {:kind "bench.find" :actions [] :filter {:repo "{{repo}},ckopsa/waymark" :path "orgs/{{org}}/**,orgkit/**,orgs/example/**,factorykit/*/org-*.edn,factorykit/*/world.edn,docs/orgkit.md,docs/spec-related-row-law.md,waymark10/*/dsl.clj,CLAUDE.md"}}
          {:kind "bench.read" :actions [] :filter {:repo "{{repo}},ckopsa/waymark" :path "orgs/{{org}}/**,orgkit/**,orgs/example/**,factorykit/*/org-*.edn,factorykit/*/world.edn,docs/orgkit.md,docs/spec-related-row-law.md,waymark10/*/dsl.clj,CLAUDE.md"}}
          {:kind "bench.edit" :actions [] :filter {:repo "{{repo}}" :path "orgs/{{org}}/**"}}
          {:kind "bench.check" :actions [] :filter {:repo "{{repo}}"}}
          {:kind "bench.test" :actions [] :filter {:repo "{{repo}}"}}
          {:kind "bench.feedback" :actions [] :filter {:repo "{{repo}}"}}
          {:kind "bench.log" :actions [] :filter {:repo "{{repo}}"}}
          {:kind "bench.pull" :actions [] :filter {:repo "{{repo}}"}}]
  ;; ticket 24c4feba: its own plan's findings cue its open sitting
  :inbox {:cues [{:kind "org_plan" :actions ["record_findings"] :filter {:name "{{org}}"} :note "Your plan's findings are in for {data.findings_sha}: read next_step."}
                 ;; ticket f9252928: the person acting on its plan's tree
                 {:kind "plan_part" :actions ["agree" "restate" "drop"] :filter {:org "{{org}}"} :note "The person acted on {data.title}: read the plan's tree and next_step."}]}}
 ;; and wake it
 :wakes [{:kind "org_plan" :actions ["record_findings"] :filter {:name "{{org}}"}}
         {:kind "plan_part" :actions ["agree" "restate" "drop"] :filter {:org "{{org}}"}}]}
